ntified the affected service** \u2014 \"payments\" initially resolved to `payments-api` (which was also showing an 18% error rate), but a human approver denied my first rollback attempt and correctly flagged that the actual faulty deploy was in `payments-worker`. Checking that service confirmed it: v3.4.0 deployed that morning was unhealthy across all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate.\n\n2. **Rolled back** `payments-worker` from v3.4.0 to its most recent healthy production release, **v3.3.0**. The rollback was approved and verified \u2014 the service is now healthy across all regions with error rate down to 0.2%.\n\n3. **Opened a SEV2 incident** (`INC-0001`) for the payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy regression; the on-call engineer was paged.\n\n**Follow-up suggestion:** The `payments-api` service is also flagged unhealthy on v5.1.0. That may be a separate issue (or downstream of the worker problem now resolved) \u2014 worth monitoring; if errors persist, consider investigating that deploy as well.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "I'll check the payments service status and its deployment history to find the last healthy release.", "reasoning_content": "Check deployments and service status first.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150c0495f750790d2b1b6", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150c0495f750790d2b1b7", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The service lookup failed for \"payments\" \u2014 the service may be registered under a different name. Let me try some common naming variants (read-only calls):", "reasoning_content": "Unknown service \"payments\