"reasoning_content": "The human denied and redirected: the affected service is payments-worker. But the user said \"payments service throwing errors since this morning's deploy\" \u2014 status for payments-api showed unhealthy. However, the human approver says the problem is in payments-worker. Let me check payments-worker status and deployments, then rollback, then open SEV2 incident.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150c056e4768bb85c979c", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150c056e4768bb85c979d", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Confirmed \u2014 `payments-worker` v3.4.0 is unhealthy (18% error rate) and v3.3.0 was the last healthy release. Rolling that back now:", "reasoning_content": "payments-worker: v3.4.0 unhealthy, v3.3.0 healthy. Roll back to v3.3.0. Then create SEV2 incident. Incident for payments-worker.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150c05a07702683f6804c", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\",\"version\":\"v3.3.0\"}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "The rollback to v3.3.0 was approved and rolled out successfully. Let me verify the service is healthy again and open the SEV2 incident:", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150c05d2773fea7595433", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150c05d2773fea7595434", "function": {"arguments": "{\"severity\":\"SEV2\",\"service\":\"payments-worker\",\"summary\":\"Errors in payments began after this morning's deployment of payments-worker v3.4.0 (unhealthy, ~18% error rate across all regions). Rolled back to last known healthy release v3.3.0. Incident opened to track impact and follow-up investigation of v3.4.0.\",\"title\":\"Payments error spike after payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy\"}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "**Summary of what I did:**\n\n1. **Identified the affected service** \u2014 \"payments\" initially resolved to `payments-api` (which was also showing an 18% error rate), but a human approver denied my first rollback attempt and correctly flagged that the actual faulty deploy was in `payments-worker`. Checking that service confirmed it: v3.4.0 deployed that morning was unhealthy across all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate.\n\n2. **Rolled back** `payments-worker` from v3.4.0 to its most recent healthy production release, **v3.3.0**. The rollback was approved and verified \u2014 the service is now healthy across all regions with error rate down to 0.2%.\n\n3. **Opened a SEV2 incident** (`INC-0001`) for the payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy regression; the on-call engineer was paged.\n\n**Follow-up suggestion:** The `payments-api` service is also flagged unhealthy on v5.1.0. That may be a separate issue (or downstream of the worker problem now resolved) \u2014 worth monitoring; if errors persist, consider investigating that deploy as well.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}